Step 1: User Request

The user selects an operation from the VS Code Command Palette, such as:

Generate Screenshot
Export JSON
Extract CSS
Accessibility Report

The extension identifies the selected task and prepares it for execution.

Step 2: Command Generation

The extension automatically generates the required Wizard command.

Example

uv run project screenshot -o homepage
uv run project accessibility
uv run project css
uv run project json

This removes the need for users to remember complex command syntax.

Step 3: Backend Communication

The generated command is sent to the backend through an API.

The extension sends:

Repository Path
Project URL
Requested Operation

The backend performs the execution and returns the generated outputs.

Step 4: Output Generation

The backend AI agent executes the requested task and generates outputs such as:

Screenshot
JSON File
CSS File
Accessibility Report

The extension receives these outputs and stores them in the project.

Step 5: Documentation

After execution, the extension automatically updates the README and Execution Verification Document (EVD) with:

Executed command
Output generated
Execution status
Logs (if available)

This ensures that every action is documented and reproducible.

